<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάρχομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make a beginning,</i> esp. in sacrifice; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίχας ἀπάρχεσθαι</span>
			<i>begin the sacrifice with</i> the hair, i.e. by cutting off the
			hair from the forehead and throwing it into the fire, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπρου ἀπὸ τρίχας ἀρξάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.254
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ὅ γ᾽ ἀπαρχόμενος τρίχας ἐν πυρὶ
					βάλλεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.422
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				3.446
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later c.
			gen., <i>cut off part</i> of a thing, <i>offer</i>
			
			<i>it,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ὠτὸς τοῦ κτήνεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.188
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κόμης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν κρεῶν καὶ σπλάγχνων</span>
			<i>offer part of</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.61
			</span></i>: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>offer the first-lings</i> or <i>first-fruits,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντων</span> of all sacrifices, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.24
			</span></i>: abs., <i>begin a sacrifice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				244
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				1056
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῖς θεοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Hier.</u>
					4.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηργμένοι,</span> of eunuchs,
				<i>having had their first-fruits offered,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				39.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>take as the first-fruits, take as the choice</i> or
				<i>best,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαστήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					767c
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>offer first-fruits,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.109
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> generally,
				<i>offer, dedicate,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσᾶς</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δραχμάς</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.652<i>B</i>19
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.406
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Theodorid.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> later, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρχομαι</span>
			, <i>begin,</i> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1409
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; <i>practise, prelude on,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργάνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Him.
					<u>Or.</u>
					17.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
